FAQ = [
    ("What size of projects do you take?",
     "Tools that one developer can deploy in weeks, not months: an admin panel, a link between two systems, a tool that replaces manual copying into a spreadsheet. For a banking system or an app for a hundred thousand users I am not the right person, and I will say so at the start."),
    ("Do we have to change the system we use?",
     "No. I almost always build next to what you already have and connect through an API or an export. Migrating a whole system is the most expensive and riskiest option, and I only suggest it when there really is no other way."),
    ("When will we see the first result?",
     "I first build the part that removes the most manual work, and you use it before everything else is finished. Then I adjust the rest based on what real use shows. That costs less than delivering something after six months that does not fit."),
    ("What if we still need you in a year?",
     "Running and further changes are a monthly fee based on the size of the tool. If you decide to carry on yourselves, you get the source code, access and documentation; I keep nothing that would force you to stay."),
    ("Where will the data live?",
     "In the European Union, on infrastructure in your name, or by agreement on my server in the Czech Republic. I process only the data the tool needs to work. Where personal data is involved, the project comes with a data processing agreement under Art. 28 GDPR."),
]

